From: Petr Stetiar <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
Subject: [PATCH] mac80211: report control port TX status on the AP encap-offload path

hostapd asks for the TX status of every EAPOL frame it sends over the
control port (NL80211_CMD_CONTROL_PORT_FRAME with a cookie). The AP
encap-offload transmit path, ieee80211_8023_xmit_ap(), stores the ack
skb for such a frame but does not set status_data_idr, unlike
ieee80211_8023_xmit() and the other users of ieee80211_store_ack_skb().
The status code reports the ack only when status_data_idr is set, so
hostapd never learns whether an EAPOL frame was acknowledged and cannot
tell "sent and not acked" from "never sent".

Set status_data_idr after storing the ack skb, as the other path does.

Throwaway debug patch for the Freedom build, never merged.

Assisted-by: claude:sonnet-5-5
Signed-off-by: Petr Stetiar <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
---
 net/mac80211/tx.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

--- a/net/mac80211/tx.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/tx.c
@@ -5188,6 +5188,9 @@ void ieee80211_8023_xmit_ap(struct ieee80211_sub_if_data *sdata,
 		info->status_data = ieee80211_store_ack_skb(local, skb,
 							    &info->flags, cookie);
 
+	if (info->status_data)
+		info->status_data_idr = 1;
+
 	info->flags |= IEEE80211_TX_CTL_HW_80211_ENCAP;
 	info->control.vif = &sdata->vif;
 	info->sawf.nw_delay = (u32) ktime_to_us(net_timedelta(skb->tstamp));
